  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019, multimodal/multiprofile/PCA/ResNet50/avgpool/weighted, acc=0.639) was built on the finding that avgpool outperformed transformer in the RNA-only multi-profile setting (0.591 vs 0.519). However, that comparison was made without an image modality present. Question: Does transformer aggregation, which can model higher-order interactions, provide a benefit in the multimodal setting where it must integrate both aggregated multi-profile RNA features and image features? This is a single-variable change from the current best (only aggregation differs), making the result directly attributable to the aggregation choice. Why this is the best next experiment: Under a limited budget, confirming or refuting the transferability of the avgpool>transformer finding to the multimodal context reduces uncertainty about a core architectural decision that will affect all future multimodal experiments. If avgpool is confirmed, we can lock it in and pivot to testing image encoder quality (ViT-L) or RNA encoder alternatives; if transformer unexpectedly helps, it reveals an important cross-modal interaction effect and reshapes the search space."
